---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro'
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro'
import { url } from '../../lib/site'

/**
 * Traducción literal de `/condiciones` (v2, MAK-254: plan mensual y programa
 * de invitaciones), sección a sección y sin resumir. `/condiciones` sigue
 * siendo la URL que Stripe pide en Settings › Public details y la que acepta
 * el cliente en el checkout, y CONDICIONES_VERSION no cambia por traducir. Si
 * cambia el texto en español, cambia esta traducción en el mismo commit.
 */
const actualizado = '24 September 2026'
---

<Base
  title="Terms of use and subscription — echo, dictation for Mac"
  description="Terms of use and subscription of echo, the dictation app for Mac by Make Algo SL."
  path="/terms"
  lang="en"
  translations={{ es: '/condiciones', en: '/terms' }}
  ogImage="/og.png"
  ogImageAlt="echo, dictation for Mac that writes it clean"
>
  <Header lang="en" />
  <main id="contenido" class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h1 style="font-size: var(--text-h2)">Terms of use and subscription</h1>
        <p class="microcopy">Last updated: {actualizado}.</p>

        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          echo is developed and sold by <strong>Make Algo SL</strong>, Tax ID (NIF) B88875018, Calle
          General Pardiñas, 114 — 28006 Madrid, Spain. You can write to us at
          <a href="mailto:hola@make-algo.com">hola@make-algo.com</a> for anything: questions,
          cancellations, complaints or exercising your rights.
        </p>
        <p>
          These terms govern downloading and using echo and, if you subscribe, the subscription. By
          installing echo you accept sections 8 to 13; by subscribing you also accept sections 4 to
          7.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What echo is and what you need to use it</h2>
        <p>
          echo is a voice dictation app for macOS: you hold a key, speak, release it and the text
          appears written in the app you were in.
        </p>
        <p>
          You need <strong>macOS 14 or later on a Mac with Apple Silicon</strong>, microphone and
          accessibility permissions, and about 600 MB of disk space for the recognition model,
          which is downloaded the first time.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AI polishing is optional</strong> and requires your own paid subscription to
          Claude (Anthropic) or ChatGPT (OpenAI), with its command-line application installed and
          signed in. <strong>We do not sell, include or broker those subscriptions.</strong> Without
          either of them, echo still works: it transcribes on your Mac and applies the voice
          punctuation commands.
        </p>

        <h2>3. What leaves your Mac and what doesn't</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Your voice never leaves.</strong> Recognition runs entirely on your Mac.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>If you turn on polishing, the transcribed text does leave.</strong> echo runs on
            your Mac the official Anthropic or OpenAI application, which sends that text
            <strong>with your own account</strong>, just as if you had pasted it into their chat
            yourself. We don't see it, receive it or store it. That transfer is governed by
            Anthropic's or OpenAI's terms and privacy policy, not by these.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>That use consumes your subscription quota</strong> with them. If you dictate a
            lot, it shows. We can't guarantee their quota will be enough for you, because it isn't
            ours.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Towards us, the only things that leave</strong> are an identifier of your Mac
            and, if you subscribe, your email address. The details are in the
            <a href={url('/privacy', 'en')}>privacy policy</a>.
          </li>
          <li>If you'd rather nothing leaves, turn polishing off in Settings.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. The 14-day trial</h2>
        <p>
          echo works in full for 14 days, free and <strong>without a card</strong>, counted from the
          first time you open it on each Mac. Once that period ends, a subscription is needed to
          keep dictating. Reinstalling does not restart the trial.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Price, payment and renewal</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The subscription comes in <strong>two options, your choice: €3 a month or €12 a
            year</strong>, VAT included in both. Either of them covers <strong>up to three
            Macs</strong> of yours; the only difference is the period and the price.
          </li>
          <li>Payment is processed by <strong>Stripe</strong>. We never see or store your card details.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>The subscription renews automatically at the end of each period</strong> —every
            month or every year, depending on the option— at the same price, unless you cancel
            before. If we are going to raise the price, we will let you know by email <strong>at
            least 30 days</strong> in advance; if it doesn't suit you, cancel before the renewal.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>You can switch options at any time</strong> —monthly to yearly or the other way
            round— from Settings › Licence, which takes you to the Stripe portal. The change is
            applied pro rata: the part of the period you have already paid for and not used is
            deducted from the new price.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>You can cancel at any time</strong>, without giving a reason, from the same
            portal. When you cancel, echo keeps working until the end of the period you have already
            paid for; there is no penalty and no minimum term.
          </li>
          <li>
            If a charge fails, we will let you know and try again. If it still can't be charged, the
            subscription is suspended.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. Right of withdrawal</h2>
        <p>
          If you are a consumer, you have the right to withdraw from the contract within
          <strong>14 calendar days</strong> without giving any reason.
        </p>
        <p>
          However: so that you can use echo as soon as you pay, when you subscribe we ask you to
          <strong>expressly consent to us starting to provide the service immediately</strong> and
          to <strong>acknowledge that, as a result, you lose the right of withdrawal</strong> once
          the service has been performed (Article 103(m) of the consolidated text of the Spanish
          General Consumer and User Protection Act). If you don't accept this, we can't activate
          your licence right away.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Regardless of the above, we give you our own money-back guarantee:</strong> if
          echo doesn't win you over, write to
          <a href="mailto:hola@make-algo.com">hola@make-algo.com</a> within <strong>14 days of your
          first charge with an amount</strong> —the first one in which you actually pay something;
          if your first charge was €0 because of a discount, the first real one counts— and we
          refund it in full, no questions asked. The guarantee covers <strong>only that first
          charge</strong>: renewals are not refunded, but you can cancel at any time and echo keeps
          working until the end of the period you have already paid for. We think that's fair,
          because you had 14 days of trial to decide beforehand.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Referral programme</h2>
        <p>
          If you have an active echo subscription taken out through Stripe, you can invite other
          people with your own code, created from Settings › Invite a friend.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>What your invitee gets:</strong> a <strong>€3 discount on their first
            charge</strong>. If they choose the monthly option, their first month is free.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>What you get:</strong> <strong>€3 of credit</strong> in your Stripe customer
            account for each invitee who goes on to pay. The credit is automatically deducted from
            your next invoices and accumulates.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>When it is credited:</strong> 14 days after your invitee's first charge with an
            amount, provided that charge has not been refunded. This matches their money-back
            guarantee under §6: the reward is credited once the payment is final.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cap:</strong> at most <strong>12 rewarded invitations per calendar year</strong>
            per person.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>Programme rules:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>The credit has no cash value.</strong> It only works as a discount on echo
            invoices: it can't be exchanged for cash, transferred or assigned to someone else. If
            your subscription ends, any unused credit is lost.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The code is for inviting other people.</strong> Self-referral —using your own
            code, or inviting yourself with another email address, another machine of yours or the
            same card— <strong>voids the reward</strong>, and we may also void rewards obtained
            through any other fraudulent or abusive use of the programme and exclude whoever does it
            from it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>We may modify or end the programme</strong>, announcing it on the website and in
            the app <strong>at least 15 days in advance</strong>. Ending it doesn't affect what you
            have already earned: you keep the credit already credited and the rewards for invitees
            who had already made their first charge with an amount before that date.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. Your licence</h2>
        <p>
          We don't sell you the software: we grant you a <strong>personal, non-exclusive,
          non-transferable and revocable licence</strong> to install and use echo on up to three
          Macs under your control, for personal or professional purposes, as long as you comply with
          these terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>You may not:</strong> resell, rent, lend, sublicense or distribute echo; remove or
          alter authorship notices; circumvent the licence check; or use echo to provide a dictation
          service to third parties who are not users of their own copies.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>You may, because the law grants it to you:</strong> make a backup copy and carry
          out the operations permitted by Article 100 of the consolidated text of the Spanish
          Intellectual Property Act, including decompilation to achieve interoperability. Nothing in
          this section limits those rights.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Third-party software and trademarks</h2>
        <p>
          echo incorporates <strong>FluidAudio</strong>, licensed under Apache 2.0, and uses
          NVIDIA's <strong>Parakeet TDT 0.6b v3</strong> recognition model, licensed under
          CC-BY-4.0. The text of both licences is in Settings › About › Licences.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Claude Code and Codex command-line applications belong to Anthropic and OpenAI
          respectively, <strong>are not distributed with echo</strong> and are governed by their own
          terms. echo is not sponsored, endorsed by or affiliated with Anthropic, OpenAI, NVIDIA or
          Apple; their trademarks are mentioned only to describe what echo works with.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Updates</h2>
        <p>
          echo periodically checks whether there is a new version and may install it. While your
          subscription is active we will provide the updates needed to keep echo in conformity with
          the contract, including security updates. You can turn off automatic installation in
          Settings; if you do and don't install the updates we offer you, we are not liable for any
          lack of conformity that is due solely to that.
        </p>

        <h2>11. If Anthropic or OpenAI change the rules</h2>
        <p>
          Polishing depends on third-party services we don't control. They may change their terms,
          prices or availability, or stop allowing this use.
        </p>
        <p>
          If that happens, <strong>we may replace the polishing provider with an equivalent
          one</strong> without it being considered a breach, notifying you by email. If none remained
          available, echo would keep working with local transcription and voice commands; if you
          consider that this amounts to a lack of conformity with what you subscribed to, you may
          terminate the subscription and we will refund the unused proportion.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Legal guarantee of conformity</h2>
        <p>
          We are liable to you for any lack of conformity of echo <strong>throughout the term of your
          subscription</strong>, in accordance with Articles 115 et seq. of the consolidated text of
          the Spanish General Consumer and User Protection Act. Nothing in these terms limits,
          excludes or conditions that guarantee. If echo doesn't do what we say it does, write to
          <a href="mailto:hola@make-algo.com">hola@make-algo.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Liability</h2>
        <p>We are liable for the foreseeable damages we cause you by breaching these terms.</p>
        <p>
          <strong>We do not exclude or limit</strong> in any case our liability for wilful
          misconduct, gross negligence, death or personal injury, or any other liability that the law
          does not allow to be limited.
        </p>
        <p>Two common-sense warnings, because they describe how echo works:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            echo <strong>pastes text into the app you are writing in</strong>. Check what appears
            before sending it. We are not responsible for the use you make of the text or for where
            it ends up.
          </li>
          <li>
            echo <strong>is not suitable for information covered by professional secrecy if you use
            polishing</strong>, because the text goes out to Anthropic or OpenAI. For those cases,
            turn polishing off.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>14. Suspension and termination</h2>
        <p>
          We may suspend or terminate your licence if the subscription is not paid or if you use echo
          in a way that breaches these terms or the law. We will notify you beforehand and give you
          a reasonable period to put it right, unless the breach is serious or urgent. You can
          terminate whenever you like by cancelling the subscription and uninstalling echo.
        </p>

        <h2>15. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may modify them for legal, technical or service-operation reasons. We will notify you by
          email <strong>at least 30 days</strong> in advance. If the changes don't suit you, you can
          cancel before they take effect and we will refund the unused proportion.
        </p>

        <h2>16. Your data</h2>
        <p>
          What we process, why, and how to exercise your rights is in the
          <a href={url('/privacy', 'en')}>privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>17. Applicable law and complaints</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by <strong>Spanish law</strong>. If you are a consumer, you keep
          the right to bring claims before the courts of your own place of residence, and the
          consumer protection laws of your country of residence in the European Union continue to
          protect you.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before going to court, write to us at
          <a href="mailto:hola@make-algo.com">hola@make-algo.com</a>: we respond to any complaint
          within one month at most.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer lang="en" otroIdiomaHref={url('/condiciones')} />
</Base>
